# fixedbugs, defect 2495, lane b34-fsl, 2026-11-13.
#
# SYMPTOM: `fixedbugs-2495-stopflag.h` declares `stop2495_requested`, which
# no header a module names defines, and two inline bodies use it: this
# module reads it through a header list that holds `stdlib.h` too, and
# `fixedbugs2495/flag_writer` writes it through the header alone. The link
# was `internal error: linking failed` at exit 2.
#
# CAUSE: a name a header's text puts in the program's objects was the
# author's only where the modules reading one header list held every
# reference, and here two lists each hold one.
#
# FIX: each list answers for the references its own modules' objects hold,
# told at its own binding (`cli/header_needs.hero`'s `holding`), the body
# that assigns the object told as writing it.
use fixedbugs2495/flag_writer

extern "stdlib.h"
    function abs(n: i32) -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-2495-stopflag.h"
    function stop2495_asked() -> i64  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    flag_writer.stop()
    print(stop2495_asked() + abs(n: -1).to_i64().must())
